      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1: Improved evidence-based policy inputs supporting pro-poor trade:
- At least 20 Policy Measures in the Trade Policy Framework implemented by 2021;
- Other Policies like E-Commerce Policy &amp; Cooperative Policy developed;
- Stakeholders sensitized on Key trade Policy related laws and regulations to enhance compliance
- New Cooperative legislation enacted by 2021

Output 1.2 : Strengthened institutional coordination of trade and development:
- At least 1 Project position established as part of MCIC organisation Structure;
- All fuel dispensers within Kiribati are verified by 2021;
- Verification equipment procured &amp; at least 15 Public Officials trained on Verification of Fuel Despensers by 2021;
- At least 20 Public Officials trained as TOT on Cooperative development;

Output 2.1: Support to boost productive capacities and access international markets:
- Processing Centre constructed and equipment procured to facilitate value addition in coconut sector;
- Mauri Mark standards for Tourism developed &amp; at least 50 producers trained on value addition techniques and market standards

Output 2.2 : Support to EIF Countries to leverage additional funding:
- At least 3 Aid-for-trade proposals developed and funded</narrative>
      </comment>
