     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1: Improved evidence-based policy inputs supporting pro-poor trade:
- At least 20 Policy Measures in the Trade Policy Framework implemented by 2021 - less than 20;
- Other Policies like E-Commerce Policy &amp; Cooperative Policy developed - in progress with consultant starting late in Qtr 4, 2021;
- Stakeholders sensitized on Key trade Policy related laws and regulations to enhance compliance - in progress
- New Cooperative legislation enacted by 2021 - in progress

Output 1.2 : Strengthened institutional coordination of trade and development:
- At least 1 Project position established as part of MCIC organization Structure - Project Manager &amp; Finance Assistant;
- All fuel dispensers within Kiribati are verified by 2021 - in progress;
- Verification equipment procured &amp; at least 15 Public Officials trained on Verification of Fuel Despensers by 2021 - none;
- At least 20 Public Officials trained as TOT on Cooperative development - none;

Output 2.1: Support to boost productive capacities and access international markets:
- Processing Centre constructed and equipment procured to facilitate value addition in coconut sector - in progress, 3-scrappers, x1 hydraulic press machine procured &amp; paid by MIE in Dec 2021 &amp; to be shipped to Kir late Jan 2022;
- Mauri Mark standards for Tourism developed &amp; at least 50 producers trained on value addition techniques and market standards - in progress

Output 2.2 : Support to EIF Countries to leverage additional funding:
- At least 3 Aid-for-trade proposals developed and funded - in progress</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
